From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crasbe <crasbe@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] md/kdf: fix undefined shift on 32 bit platforms

Shifting a 32 bit size_t by 32 bits is undefined behavior. Newer compilers
(e.g. clang 20) exploit this and miscompile nist_kdf() on 32 bit platforms,
resulting in a segfault. Cast key_len to uint64_t before shifting.

This has to be fixed upstream: https://github.com/relic-toolkit/relic/issues/318

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 src/md/relic_md_kdf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/md/relic_md_kdf.c b/src/md/relic_md_kdf.c
index fc26653..b1aec89 100644
--- a/src/md/relic_md_kdf.c
+++ b/src/md/relic_md_kdf.c
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ static void nist_kdf(uint8_t *key, size_t key_len, const uint8_t *in,
 	uint8_t *buffer = NULL, hash[RLC_MD_LEN];
 	size_t out_len = 0;
 
-	if (((key_len >> 32) > RLC_MD_LEN) ||
+	if ((((uint64_t)key_len >> 32) > RLC_MD_LEN) ||
 		(in_len + sizeof(uint32_t) < in_len)) {
 		RLC_THROW(ERR_NO_VALID);
 		return;
-- 
